===============================================================================
DeepStream Service-Maker — Reusable Python Probe Modules
===============================================================================

This directory contains Python probe modules that can be attached to pipeline
elements as lightweight glue logic. Each module uses the @probe decorator to
register itself in CommonFactory under a name string. Once registered, the
probe is indistinguishable from a compiled C++ probe plugin — it can be used
in YAML config or the direct pipeline API.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
How to use a Python probe module
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Add the modules directory to sys.path and import the module:

     import sys
     sys.path.insert(0, "/opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/service-maker/modules/python")
     import sample_video_probe  # registers "sample_video_probe" in CommonFactory

2a. YAML config — declare as a pipeline node with type "python.<name>":

     - type: python.sample_video_probe
       name: svp
       properties:
         font-size: 18

2b. Direct API — attach by registered name:

     pipeline.attach("infer", "sample_video_probe", "svp",
                     properties={"font-size": 18})

For a complete working example see:
  <install_dir>/service-maker/sources/apps/python/pipeline_api/deepstream_python_probe_app/

===============================================================================
Available Modules
===============================================================================

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
sample_video_probe
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Counts vehicles and persons detected per frame and overlays the result as
  text on the OSD display.

  Attach point: nvinfer (or any element after object detection)

  Parameters:
    font-size  integer  12   size of the font for the counter text overlay

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
measure_fps_probe
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Measures pipeline throughput and prints frames-per-second to stdout at a
  configurable interval.

  Attach point: any pipeline element

  Parameters:
    interval   integer  5    FPS reporting interval in seconds

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
measure_latency_probe
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Measures and prints end-to-end pipeline latency per frame to stdout.

  Attach point: any pipeline element (typically the sink-side element)

  Parameters: none

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
kitti_dump_probe
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Dumps object detection or tracker results to KITTI-format label files on
  disk, one file per frame.

  Attach point: nvinfer or nvtracker

  Parameters:
    kitti-dir             string   "/tmp/kitti"   output directory for KITTI label files
    tracker-kitti-output  boolean  false          use tracker bbox/confidence instead
                                                  of detector output

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
add_message_meta_probe
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Attaches DeepStream event message metadata to frames so that downstream
  messaging plugins (nvmsgconv + nvmsgbroker) can forward events to Kafka,
  MQTT, or other message brokers.

  Attach point: nvinfer or nvtracker

  Parameters:
    frame-interval  integer  1    generate event metadata every N frames
    source-config   string   ""   path to source config YAML
    label-file      string   ""   path to label file (one label per line)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
resnet_tensor_parser
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Parses raw ResNet detector output tensors and populates NvDsObjectMeta in
  the pipeline. Use this when nvinfer is configured with output-tensor-meta=1
  and you want custom post-processing in Python instead of a C++ parser.

  Attach point: nvinfer (output-tensor-meta mode)

  Parameters:
    network-width   integer  960   model input width
    network-height  integer  544   model input height
    stream-width    integer  1280  source stream width
    stream-height   integer  720   source stream height
    num-classes     integer  4     number of detection classes
